From: nuubOS Project
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: pwrseq_simple: fall back to GPIO reset on -ENOENT

Some GPIO controllers, including the Allwinner sunxi GPIO controller,
use more than two GPIO cells. The generic reset-gpio controller
currently supports only GPIO providers using two cells.

When mmc-pwrseq-simple has a single reset-gpios entry it first tries
to acquire it through the reset controller API. On unsupported GPIO
providers this can return -ENOENT, causing the power sequence probe
to fail before the existing GPIO fallback can be used.

Treat -ENOENT as an unavailable reset controller and continue with
the GPIO-based reset path. Other errors, including probe deferral,
are still propagated.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS Project
---
 drivers/mmc/core/pwrseq_simple.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/core/pwrseq_simple.c b/drivers/mmc/core/pwrseq_simple.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/core/pwrseq_simple.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/pwrseq_simple.c
@@ -132,9 +132,13 @@ static int mmc_pwrseq_simple_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	ngpio = of_count_phandle_with_args(dev->of_node, "reset-gpios", "#gpio-cells");
 	if (ngpio == 1) {
 		pwrseq->reset_ctrl = devm_reset_control_get_optional_shared(dev, NULL);
-		if (IS_ERR(pwrseq->reset_ctrl))
+		if (IS_ERR(pwrseq->reset_ctrl) &&
+		    PTR_ERR(pwrseq->reset_ctrl) != -ENOENT)
 			return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(pwrseq->reset_ctrl),
 					     "reset control not ready\n");
+
+		if (IS_ERR(pwrseq->reset_ctrl))
+			pwrseq->reset_ctrl = NULL;
 	}

 	/*
